@prefix sentinel: <http://example.org/orexis/firmware/moisture-sentinel#> .
@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/firmware/moisture-sentinel#> .
@prefix sensing: <http://example.org/orexis/sensing#> .
@prefix mc:   <http://example.org/orexis/microcontroller#> .
@prefix ag:   <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix ssn:  <http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/orexis/firmware/moisture-sentinel> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "The sentinel — what a board running this firmware IS" ;
    rdfs:comment """The second firmware's self-description (#175); see the governed node's for
the pattern. The temperaments differ in every fact stated here, which is the point of stating
them here: one flashed image, one set of promises, however many boards run it.""" .

:Node a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "sentinel" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ag:Device ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty sensing:senseMode ;
          owl:hasValue sensing:PushProcedure ] ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty mc:firmware ;
          owl:hasValue "moisture-sentinel" ] ,
        #  Unlike the governed node, the alarm promise is UNCONDITIONAL here: a sentinel's
        #  whole reason to exist is the vigil its ULP keeps, so every board of this kind
        #  implements the procedure — on the class, because there is no flashing this
        #  firmware without it. What that vigil WATCHES changed (movement, not the world's
        #  range); that there is one did not, which is why this restriction still stands.
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty ssn:implements ;
          owl:hasValue sensing:AlarmProcedure ] ;
    rdfs:comment "A board that answers to nobody: it takes no orders — no command channel, nothing to parse — so its agent derives Listening and can only receive. Its ULP watches for MOVEMENT, the last published value plus or minus a deviation limit, and wakes it to speak when the reading leaves that window; a slow heartbeat generated under its agent's freshness rule keeps silence distinguishable from death. It does NOT watch the world's operating range, though the range still sizes the deviation limit — see knowledge/decisions/the-sentinel-alarms-on-movement.md for why watching it made a thirsty pot wake the radio every patrol forever." .
